    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d594">

                <pb facs="0673" n="655" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg655"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.248/1–2146: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wiley</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-01-21T11:00:00-05:00">January 21, 1946—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:21 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>72. Deptel 48, January 18, 8 p.m. and Embtel 68, January 20, 8 a.m. Agreement
                    reached by General Arnold covers following planes for delivery prior to 30
                    April: 3 B–25’s, 8 P–47’s, 2 C–45’s (or AT–7’s), 5 AT–11’s, 2 AT–6’s, 15 PT’s, 2
                    OA’s; and for immediate delivery 3 C–47’s and 2 PBY’s.<anchor n="19"
                        xml:id="d594-f1"/></p>
                <p>General Arnold stressed importance that Latin America and US “speak the same
                    language” in respect of equipment, operations and maintenance and made generous
                    offers with regard to admitting Colombian officers to American Air Force
                    schools. General Piedrahita will submit list of 60 young officers in March and
                    some 18 other officers of higher rank to proceed for this purpose to US.</p>
                <p>I approve heartily.…</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wiley</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d594-f1" n="19" xml:id="d594-f1-content">
                <p>A marginal note reads: “This is not in accord with ‘Adjusted Requirements’ table,
                    so I assume that this represents Col. Govt’s modification? B. C. D[avis]”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
